WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.020
Speaker 1: We have some interesting news on the&nbsp;
fight to remove George Anthony Davis elder Santos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:14.160
from the House of Representatives. House Democrats&nbsp;
have filed a resolution led by Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:21.840
Congressman Robert Garcia to expel yes, to expel&nbsp;
Jorge Santos from the House of Representatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:30.300
It is the latest escalation, writes Axios, of&nbsp;
Democrats efforts to punish Santos for the serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:37.200
fabrications about his background. I have not&nbsp;
been super familiar with Congressman Robert Garcia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.740
up until now. He has an unbelievable sense of&nbsp;
timing. Listen to this interview in which he says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:51.349
you know, Santos is a lot like me, Latino, gay,&nbsp;
except he lies about everything. This is so funny.&nbsp;

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:57.060
Speaker 5: As an openly gay person, as an&nbsp;
immigrant, as a Latino. I look at Mr. Santos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.420
as someone who is actually very similar to&nbsp;
me, except that he lies about everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:06.720
And so within within our own LGBTQ community,&nbsp;
there's like major disgust in what he's doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.060
and his representation of our community. And&nbsp;
so it's not acceptable for him to lie about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:19.140
every single part of his past, including now&nbsp;
getting classified information or access to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.000
So it's just it's time that honest. The final&nbsp;
straw was getting access to giving, actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.420
being given access to classified information. He&nbsp;
was literally getting someone as a primary wire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.740
access to America's secrets in the media.
Speaker 1: Yeah. So, of course, I agree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:37.200
completely with Robert Garcia. I would not. A few&nbsp;
of you emailed me after the story broke and said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.100
David, this is such a waste of time. Republicans&nbsp;
control the House of Representatives. There is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:47.700
just no way in hell that this goes anywhere.&nbsp;
You know, you're probably right. But it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:55.920
true that there are some Republicans who are&nbsp;
disgusted by Jorge Santos, and they've said it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.580
If Mitt Romney were in the House of&nbsp;
Representatives rather than the Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:06.960
I am 100% sure that Romney would join Democrats&nbsp;
in a vote to remove George Santos. So because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.080
majority for Republicans is quite small, it is not&nbsp;
completely out of the question that you find that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:18.840
Democrats find just enough Republicans to maybe&nbsp;
get rid of George Santos. Do I think it's the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:26.100
likely outcome? No. But is this worth doing and&nbsp;
try to get a vote and try to get Republicans on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:32.940
the record, get them to say, no, I vote for Santos&nbsp;
to stay. I actually do think it's a good idea in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:40.200
this particular case. Now, I am not someone who,&nbsp;
as a blanket says, symbolic votes in the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:46.680
are either worth it or not worth that wastes of&nbsp;
time or good uses of time. I don't have a generic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:54.540
umbrella view on that. I am balancing in my&nbsp;
assessment. Is it really guaranteed to be symbolic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.640
only or is there actually a chance that you might&nbsp;
pass it? What would we achieve by putting members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.720
on the record, by getting them to vote one way&nbsp;
or another? You know, when we think back to that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:08.460
force, the vote, Medicare for All thing, we&nbsp;
really knew the positions of basically every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:14.160
every member of Congress on that issue. I actually&nbsp;
don't know the positions of every member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.900
House on whether they would vote to keep or expel&nbsp;
George Santos. And it actually is a close enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.920
margin now that it that at least theoretically it&nbsp;
could work. I think this is an interesting idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:27.480
Good for Robert Garcia, Good for Democrats.&nbsp;
Let's see if we ultimately get a vote on it

